From: Daniel Martin <dmanlfc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: aw88166: quieten the remaining log spam

On top of ROCKNIX's reduce-log-spam patch, which leaves two messages at
error level. Both fire for the same reason as the rest: the amp is probed
or stopped while no I2S clock is running, which is normal while idle.
The patch's own "start failure" error still reports a genuine failure.
---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/aw88166.c	2026-09-22 00:13:42.834085887 +1000
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/aw88166.c	2026-09-22 00:13:42.892665223 +1000
@@ -180,7 +180,7 @@
 		dev_dbg(aw_dev->dev, "mode1 check iis failed try switch to mode2 check");
 		ret = aw_dev_check_mode2_pll(aw_dev);
 		if (ret) {
-			dev_err(aw_dev->dev, "mode2 check iis failed");
+			dev_dbg(aw_dev->dev, "mode2 check iis failed");
 			return ret;
 		}
 	}
@@ -1220,7 +1220,7 @@
 
 	aw_dev_get_int_status(aw_dev, &reg_val);
 	if (reg_val & AW88166_BIT_SYSINT_CHECK) {
-		dev_err(aw_dev->dev, "pa stop check fail:0x%04x\n", reg_val);
+		dev_dbg(aw_dev->dev, "pa stop check fail:0x%04x\n", reg_val);
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
